---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/legal.css';

const company = 'Subliminal Design System LLC';
const address = '440 Monticello Ave Ste 1802 #625273, Norfolk, VA 23510, United States';
const email = 'support@subliminaldesignsystem.com';
const updated = 'November 11, 2026';

// The numbered sections below, in order, for the table of contents.
const sections = [
  { id: 'acceptance-of-terms', title: 'Acceptance of Terms' },
  { id: 'changes-to-the-terms', title: 'Changes to the Terms' },
  { id: 'using-the-site', title: 'Using the Site' },
  { id: 'intellectual-property-and-open-source-software', title: 'Intellectual Property and Open-Source Software' },
  { id: 'feedback', title: 'Feedback' },
  { id: 'third-party-links', title: 'Third-Party Links' },
  { id: 'disclaimers', title: 'Disclaimers' },
  { id: 'limitation-of-liability', title: 'Limitation of Liability' },
  { id: 'suspension-and-termination', title: 'Suspension and Termination' },
  { id: 'governing-law-and-disputes', title: 'Governing Law and Disputes' },
  { id: 'general', title: 'General' },
  { id: 'contact-us', title: 'Contact Us' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service · Subliminal Design System"
  description="The terms for using subliminaldesignsystem.com."
>
  <article class="policy">
    <header class="title-block">
      <h1 class="sds-text--title-huge">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="sds-text--content-large updated">Updated: {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <h2 id="welcome" class="sds-text--title-small">Welcome to Our Terms of Service</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-large lead">
      These Terms of Service (the “Terms”) govern your use of subliminaldesignsystem.com (the “Site”),
      which is operated by {company} (“we,” “us,” or “our”). By using the Site you agree to the
      Terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the Site. The Site is a documentation website. If
      we add accounts, a newsletter, or paid features, additional terms will apply to them, and we
      will publish those terms before the features launch.
    </p>

    <nav aria-label="Table of contents" class="toc">
      <h2 class="sds-text--title-xsmall">Table of contents</h2>
      <ol class="sds-text--interactive-medium">
        {sections.map((section) => (
          <li><a href={`#${section.id}`}>{section.title}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="acceptance-of-terms" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      By accessing or using the Site you confirm that you have read and agree to these Terms and to
      our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. You must be at least 16 years old to use the Site.
      If you use the Site on behalf of an organization, you confirm that you are allowed to accept
      these Terms for it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes-to-the-terms" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">2. Changes to the Terms</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      We may update these Terms from time to time. The date at the top shows when they last changed.
      If we make a material change, we will say so clearly on the Site. If you keep using the Site
      after a change takes effect, you accept the updated Terms.
    </p>

    <h2 id="using-the-site" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">3. Using the Site</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      You may read the Site, link to it, and use what it teaches you in your own work. You agree not
      to:
    </p>
    <ul class="sds-text--content-medium">
      <li>break the law, or help anyone else to, through your use of the Site;</li>
      <li>interfere with or disrupt the Site, its hosting, or other people's use of it, including by
        sending automated traffic at a volume that affects its performance;</li>
      <li>try to gain unauthorized access to the Site, its infrastructure, or other people's data; or</li>
      <li>probe the Site for security weaknesses other than by reporting what you find to us
        privately at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="intellectual-property-and-open-source-software" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">4. Intellectual Property and Open-Source Software</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      The Site's text, graphics, layout, name, and logo belong to us or our licensors and are
      protected by intellectual property laws. These Terms let you view and link to the Site. They do
      not give you any right to use our name or logo, or to present anything as coming from or
      endorsed by us, without our written permission.
    </p>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      The Subliminal Design System software (the code in its public repository and its published
      package) is licensed separately, under the open-source licence in that repository. That
      licence, not these Terms, governs your use of the code, and nothing here limits the rights it
      gives you. The fonts used on the Site, Manrope and Work Sans, are licensed under the SIL Open
      Font License 1.1.
    </p>

    <h2 id="feedback" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">5. Feedback</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      If you send us suggestions or feedback, we may use them without limit and without owing you
      anything, and without any obligation to keep them confidential. Please don't send us anything
      you want to keep private.
    </p>

    <h2 id="third-party-links" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">6. Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      The Site may link to websites and services that we don't own or control. We are not responsible
      for them, and linking to one is not an endorsement. Their own terms and privacy policies apply
      to your use of them.
    </p>

    <h2 id="disclaimers" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">7. Disclaimers</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      The Site and everything on it are provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of
      any kind, whether express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
      particular purpose, non-infringement, accuracy, and uninterrupted or error-free operation.
      Design guidance, tokens, and examples are provided for information only: you are responsible
      for testing anything you build with them, including for accessibility and legal compliance in
      your own products.
    </p>

    <h2 id="limitation-of-liability" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special,
      consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue, data, or goodwill, arising
      out of or related to your use of the Site, even if we have been told they are possible. To the
      fullest extent the law allows, our total liability for all claims relating to the Site will not
      exceed US$100. Nothing in these Terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited, such as
      liability for fraud, or for death or personal injury caused by negligence, and nothing in them
      takes away consumer rights that cannot be waived in your country.
    </p>

    <h2 id="suspension-and-termination" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">9. Suspension and Termination</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      We may suspend or restrict access to the Site at any time, for example if we think these Terms
      have been broken or to protect the Site's security, and we may change or discontinue the Site.
      Sections 4, 5, 7, 8, 10, and 11 continue to apply after your use of the Site ends.
    </p>

    <h2 id="governing-law-and-disputes" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">10. Governing Law and Disputes</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the Commonwealth of Virginia, United States, without
      regard to its conflict-of-law rules. Any dispute arising out of or relating to these Terms or
      the Site will be brought in the state or federal courts located in Virginia, and you and we
      consent to their jurisdiction. If you are a consumer, this does not take away any protection
      you have under the mandatory laws of the country where you live, or any right to bring a claim
      in the courts of that country.
    </p>

    <h2 id="general" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">11. General</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      These Terms and our Privacy Policy are the whole agreement between you and us about the Site.
      If a part of them is found to be unenforceable, the rest stays in effect. If we don't enforce a
      part of them, that is not a waiver of it. We may assign these Terms in connection with a sale or
      reorganization of the business; you may not assign them without our consent.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact-us" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">12. Contact Us</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      If you have a question about these Terms, contact us at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>, or write to:
    </p>
    <address class="sds-text--content-medium">
      {company}<br />
      {address}
    </address>
  </article>
</Layout>
